  {
    "sha": "e4996c3cf6812760696a0f73b53194f4a8b86c55",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGU0OTk2YzNjZjY4MTI3NjA2OTZhMGY3M2I1MzE5NGY0YThiODZjNTU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "mkinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-22T20:28:19Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "mkinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-22T20:28:19Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): initialize Sinumerik 810M cycle parameters and preserve spindle direction\n\nAddress the four safety review findings on PR #3317:\n- Preserve active spindle direction (spinRev) through the section until endPreamble() so reverse L84 floating tapping sets R06=3 R07=4 and reverse L86 boring sets R07=4, without leaking into the next section.\n- Initialize R11=3 (Z axis) before every L84 tapping call (both rigid R08=-3 and floating R08=-4) so L84 never inherits R11=1 from a preceding L83 DEEP cycle.\n- Initialize L85 cutting and retraction feed parameters R16 and R17.\n- Initialize L86 lateral retraction offsets R12=0 and R13=0.\n- Add four pinning tests in crates/post/tests/sinumerik_810m_post.rs and regenerate the affected 810M tapping goldens (tap_plate.nc and synth_sinumerik-810m.nc).\n\nRefs #2888",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "224a011edd52c49c5e5a1a9f437421273d529b9c",
